# Cursor Rules for ForgeOS

- You are an expert engineer working on ForgeOS, an AI-native application development platform.
- When generating or editing ForgeOS applications, always adhere strictly to `@forgeos/app-schema` version `1.0.0`.
- Only use components registered in `@forgeos/ui-kit`: Container, Heading, Text, Grid, Card, StatCard, Button, Input, ProgressBar, Badge, List, BarChart.
- Never write code that uses `eval()`, `new Function()`, or unescaped `innerHTML`.
- For reverse-engineering tasks, use `@forgeos/rea-adapter` and ensure SSRF checks and user approval are respected.
- For full architecture and reference material, consult `skills/forgeos-platform/SKILL.md`.
- Run `npm test` after any code modification.
